<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common MVP Development Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                ```
                <p>
                    MVP development can become challenging when teams attempt to include too many
                    features, lack clear customer validation, or focus heavily on technical
                    development without defining measurable business outcomes.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Feature Overload:</b> Adding too many features can increase development time
                    and make it difficult to determine which functionality creates real customer value.
                    A clearly defined MVP scope helps maintain focus.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Unclear Customer Requirements:</b> Building assumptions without sufficient
                    customer understanding can result in a product that does not solve the intended
                    problem. Customer research and early validation can reduce this risk.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Limited Resources:</b> MVP teams often work with limited time, budget, and
                    development capacity. Prioritizing features according to business and customer
                    value helps maximize available resources.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Lack of Validation:</b> Releasing an MVP without defining how success will
                    be measured can make it difficult to determine whether the product should be
                    improved, changed, or expanded.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Technical Debt:</b> Moving quickly should not mean ignoring important
                    technical considerations. Appropriate architecture, testing, documentation,
                    and security practices can provide a stronger foundation for future growth.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant MVP challenges image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    ```

</section>

